/-!
# The six rank-three small even Frattini models

Each candidate has a checked finite model, a surjective map to the displayed
binary quotient, and a kernel generated by its explicit square words. The
order-centralizer fiber counts use exactly the basis of `rankThreeProfile`.

Source: the Shinoda (1975), (2.3), pp. 81–82 root convention, through the
verified group operations in `Core`, `RootAction`, and `Sylow`.
-/

namespace ReeTwo.SylowModel.SmallEvenAutB

/-- All six rank-three candidates realize the prescribed Frattini profiles. -/
public theorem rankThreeModels (i : Fin 6) : RankThreeModel i := by
  fin_cases i
  · exact C24.model
  · exact C25.model
  · exact C38.model
  · exact C43.model
  · exact C46.model
  · exact C51.model

end ReeTwo.SylowModel.SmallEvenAutB
